WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.420
Lance Reddick might be gone, but the legendary&nbsp;
actor will never be forgotten. The cast of "John&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:10.740
Wick 4" took time during the premiere of the&nbsp;
film to pay tribute to their departed friend.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:15.900
Lance Reddick, who played the Continental&nbsp;
Hotel's slick and savvy concierge Charon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:22.680
died on March 17 2023, aged 60. Reddick&nbsp;
appeared in all four "John Wick" films&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:27.720
and is slated to appear in the upcoming Ana&nbsp;
de Armas-led franchise spin-off "Ballerina."

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:32.580
Variety reports that attendees of the Los&nbsp;
Angeles premiere of "John Wick 4" were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:38.100
asked to wear a blue ribbon pin upon entering&nbsp;
the TCL Chinese Theatre. Blue was Reddick's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:43.440
favorite color. All of the event's attendees,&nbsp;
including lead star Keanu Reeves and director&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:48.660
Chad Stahelski had their snaps taken with the&nbsp;
simple but beautiful tribute. While speaking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:53.100
with star Laurence Fishburne, Entertainment&nbsp;
Tonight noted that Reddick's character poster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.880
was the first one to greet attendees at&nbsp;
the "Chapter 4" premiere. In general,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:02.160
the atmosphere at the premiere was celebratory&nbsp;
but solemn. Fishburne told ET at the premiere,

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.800
"We lost our brother. We lost our brother."

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.280
Reeves also praised the late&nbsp;
actor during the red carpet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:13.740
describing Reddick as a "people person" and&nbsp;
"special artist" while speaking with Variety.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:17.880
"It's just really something special,&nbsp;
every time he stepped on set,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.840
to watch the passion he had for his&nbsp;
work. It's really easy to work with him."

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:24.968
As Reeves succinctly put it&nbsp;
while talking to Deadline,

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:27.413
"f–king sucks he's not here."

00:01:27.413 --> 00:01:30.060
The love and respect for Reddick&nbsp;
and his "John Wick" character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:32.734
continued inside the screening room as well.

00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:40.544
"And as always, it's a&nbsp;
pleasure to have you with us again, Mr. Wick."

00:01:40.544 --> 00:01:45.420
Before Keanu Reeves and director Chad Stahelski&nbsp;
took to the stage to introduce the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:48.960
The Hollywood Reporter noted that&nbsp;
President of the Lionsgate Motion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:53.520
Picture Group Joe Drake paid tribute to&nbsp;
Lance Reddick. Drake said to applause,

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.980
"It would be impossible to not acknowledge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:59.100
how profoundly sad we are by&nbsp;
the loss of Lance Reddick."

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:04.680
The executive then acknowledged how impactful the&nbsp;
loss of Reddick was. In honor of the late actor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:08.340
Drake implored those in the auditorium&nbsp;
to celebrate the actor with applause.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:12.120
"Tonight, what I would like to do,&nbsp;
however, is to ask you to make loud,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:16.980
honoring, grateful applause for a man who&nbsp;
was an absolutely extraordinary human being,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:20.700
extraordinary actor, and a&nbsp;
big part of this franchise."

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:24.540
Reddick received a standing ovation&nbsp;
from those in the cinema hall.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:28.620
"John Wick: Chapter 4" screened after&nbsp;
an introduction by both Keanu Reeves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:32.400
and Chad Stahelski. Variety,&nbsp;
in attendance at the premiere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:36.840
noted that Lance Reddick's first appearance&nbsp;
in the film received considerable applause&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:41.760
from viewers. Shortly after the film's&nbsp;
premiere, Deadline confirmed that "John Wick:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:46.200
Chapter 4" was dedicated in Reddick's&nbsp;
memory. Stahelski told Variety,

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:49.320
"I just got to be happy and&nbsp;
be proud of the fact that I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.320
got to spend so much time with&nbsp;
him. We're going to miss him."

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:56.520
While Reddick was widely celebrated&nbsp;
for his decade-long stint in John Wick,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:01.740
the actor is also remembered for his starring&nbsp;
role in "The Wire." After his death was confirmed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:06.660
"The Wire" creator David Simon took to&nbsp;
social media to praise the actor, tweeting,

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:12.240
"Consummate professional, devoted collaborator,&nbsp;
lovely and gentle man, loyal friend."

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:15.360
In addition to his roles on&nbsp;
the big and small screen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:19.020
Reddick was an integral part of&nbsp;
Bungie's "Destiny" video game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:24.060
where he played Commander Zavala. The hours&nbsp;
following his passing, thousands of "Destiny"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:29.400
players took to Zavala's in-game location to&nbsp;
pay tribute to the actor. The act of kindness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:34.200
and support was later commended in an official&nbsp;
statement by Lance Reddick's wife, Stephanie.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:38.880
The latest "John Wick" film is Reddick's&nbsp;
first posthumous role. The actor will next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:43.500
be seen in Hulu's remake of "White Men&nbsp;
Can't Jump" and will headline Disney+'s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:46.920
adaptation of "Percy Jackson&nbsp;
and the Olympians" as Zeus.

